Oh wait! I see the issue now. When `fgetc` returns EOF and `feof(fp)` is true, I break out of the while loop. Then I set `buf[len] = '\0'` and return `buf`. But if `len == 0`, this creates an empty string. On the next call to `read_line`, it allocates a new buffer, reads EOF immediately, breaks, and returns another empty string. This continues forever!

